      "start_seconds": 1.18,
      "end_seconds": 4.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "morning, doctor. Is this the right room?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.86,
      "end_seconds": 12.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "you're alright, take a seat what can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.04,
      "end_seconds": 21.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "so, so the the thing is, I've got pain in the lower left tummy"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.8,
      "end_seconds": 25.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "how many days or weeks has it it been?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.46,
      "end_seconds": 29.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "it's been about four days now"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.38,
      "end_seconds": 39.94,
      "duration_seconds": 9.56,
      "text": "Ah. Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.09,
      "end_seconds": 49.98,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "it feels moderate to me. I'd say all the time. I notice it more with moving"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.93,
      "end_seconds": 57.39,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "does anything else come with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 58.5,
      "end_seconds": 67.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.91,
      "text": "It usually comes with constipation then loose stools. The constipation then loose stools? That's been since last Tuesday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.64,
      "end_seconds": 76.37,
      "duration_seconds": 7.73,
      "text": "Okay, have you had pain in the lower left tummy before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.98,
      "end_seconds": 83.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "so, I had a similar thing last year it went away"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.37,
      "end_seconds": 97.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Any vomiting or blood in the stool at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 98.39,
      "end_seconds": 103.32,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Um no no vomiting or blood in the stool."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.3,
      "end_seconds": 110.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "let me check a few things any urinary symptoms or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.98,
      "end_seconds": 113.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "no, I'd have said so so"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 114.45,
      "end_seconds": 116.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "How's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 118.12,
      "end_seconds": 120.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "no my breathing's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 122.58,
      "end_seconds": 124.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "Has your skin been okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.8,
      "end_seconds": 128.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "actually, nothing on the skin, no"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.34,
      "end_seconds": 144.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "right, what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.8,
      "end_seconds": 155.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "Heart disease for five years. Yes an enlarged prostate. Work has been very busy so I kept ignoring it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.96,
      "end_seconds": 162.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "Okay, what else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 163.97,
      "end_seconds": 177.47,
      "duration_seconds": 13.5,
      "text": "right, so heart disease and an enlarged prostate are already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 178.67,
      "end_seconds": 188.79,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "My partner and our baby. I retired from the post office two years ago. I do a yoga class on Thursdays"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.77,
      "end_seconds": 192.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "let's run through your medicines"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.54,
      "end_seconds": 204.93,
      "duration_seconds": 12.39,
      "text": "Um, you know, it's aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day for my heart. I'm supposed to take it regularly, but I don't always manage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.96,
      "end_seconds": 208.93,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.8,
      "end_seconds": 220.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "bear with me while this finishes.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.62,
      "end_seconds": 245.92,
      "duration_seconds": 8.3,
      "text": "okay: pulse 101 pressure 104 over 76 temperature is 39.1 degrees respiratory rate 19 SpO2 96 percent on room air"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.86,
      "end_seconds": 250.61,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "right, is that alright, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.59,
      "end_seconds": 259.41,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "they help me see the whole picture, more shortly"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.76,
      "end_seconds": 264.45,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 265.94,
      "end_seconds": 267.92,
      "duration_seconds": 1.98,
      "text": "raise your arm for me"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.95,
      "end_seconds": 287.71,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "it is tender in the lower left with no guarding or rigidity"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.92,
      "end_seconds": 293.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "That's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.01,
      "end_seconds": 308.04,
      "duration_seconds": 5.03,
      "text": "right here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is acute diverticulitis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 309.42,
      "end_seconds": 310.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.3,
      "end_seconds": 342.61,
      "duration_seconds": 30.31,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now acute diverticulitis is my leading thought, not anything worse. I'd like to arrange a CT scan for left iliac fossa pain. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Blood tests is what I'd like next, for abdominal pain. For this, co-amoxiclav, 625 milligrams, three times a day, five days. You take it by mouth. That should help with diverticulitis"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 344.41,
      "end_seconds": 349.12,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "okay, so alright, I'll pick it up today"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 349.98,
      "end_seconds": 353.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.86,
      "text": "drink plenty and start with a a light diet"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.43,
      "end_seconds": 360.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.23,
      "text": "yes one warning sign to remember: the symptoms get worse in that case don't wait"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 362.28,
      "end_seconds": 363.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "alright, I follow"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 365.64,
      "end_seconds": 371.32,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "book a a review in one week have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
